  "reading": "A trip never visits the same corridor twice among the tested corridors, so a trip cannot cluster a corridor's own legs, and the creation day is nearly independent of the statistic. The cluster that does bind a corridor's legs is the recurring service (route_schedule_uuid): legs of one corridor and one schedule are alike (see the schedule-cell ICC and design effect). Caveat: a majority of the corridors run under a single schedule, where the corridor effect and the service effect cannot be told apart, and the within-corridor ICC estimate is biased downward by demeaning on the corridor; the design effect is a lower-bound guide."
